  "unknowns": [
    {
      "id": "U-01",
      "question": "What HTTP status and message does a duration violation return? Line 190 gives gate TIME_WINDOW and rule_reference \"TSD-4 §3\", and lines 18/30 associate rule_reference/failing_gate with a 422 response, but the duration rule itself states neither the status code nor the message text.",
      "affects": ["EP-01", "EP-03", "BV-01", "BV-02"]
    },
    {
      "id": "U-02",
      "question": "How is window_end at or before window_start reported? Is it the same TIME_WINDOW failure with rule_reference \"TSD-4 §3\" (\"Duration out of range\"), or is it refused earlier, when the request is written (for example a 400), before any gate runs? The spec does not say, and it also doesn't say whether window_end = window_start + 1 minute is reported as the 15-minute violation.",
      "affects": ["EP-05", "BV-03"]
    },
    {
      "id": "U-03",
      "question": "At what precision is duration compared? Can window_start/window_end carry seconds (for example 14 min 59 s or 240 min 30 s), and if so are they rounded, truncated or compared exactly?",
      "affects": ["BV-01", "BV-02", "BV-03"]
    },
    {
      "id": "U-04",
      "question": "How are missing, null, malformed or non-UTC-offset window_start/window_end values handled? The spec only says they are stored and compared in UTC (line 101).",
      "affects": []
    },
    {
      "id": "U-05",
      "question": "In what order are the TIME_WINDOW conditions checked? If a window breaks the duration rule and also another TIME_WINDOW condition (lead time, advance booking, curfew, overlap), which rule_reference is returned? Line 30 only fixes the order between gates.",
      "affects": ["EP-01", "EP-03", "EP-05", "BV-01", "BV-02", "BV-03"]
    },
    {
      "id": "U-06",
      "question": "When is the duration rule evaluated: on validate, on submit, when the draft is created or updated, or on all of these? The spec does not name the operation, so the tests can't yet say where to send the window.",
      "affects": ["EP-01", "EP-02", "EP-03", "EP-04", "EP-05", "BV-01", "BV-02", "BV-03"]
    }
  ]
}
